it's that time of the year again and  what better way to get into the  christmas and holiday spirit than by  taking a look at some of its weirdest  and most terrifying legends  okay so i can think of about a dozen  better ways but at least i can share  this one with you  in store today we have all sorts of  weird stories from crazy goblins a child  eating giantess her also giant killer  cat and much more  before we delve any deeper a quick word  from today's sponsor scentbird the  fragrance-based subscription service  that is a perfect gift for any occasion  if you give someone a scent bird  subscription as a gift they can pick out  the fragrances they want to try so  instead of paying full price for a  perfume or cologne they've never smelt  before they receive a sample for a  fraction of the price the scentbird  vials are not your average testers which  are gone in two or three sprays they are  eight times larger which is enough for  30 days if a subscription service isn't  for them scentbird also has a host of  gift boxes to choose from with all the  best-selling brands such as dolce  gabbana gucci calvin klein and many more  they have fragrances for both men and  women as well as a selection of unisex  options if you decide to treat someone  or even yourself to a scentbird  subscription then use code mfe30  to get 30 of your first month  subscription which means you only pay  about 11  it's also now available in canada  we start today with our first of three  stories that originate from iceland who  seem to be more than fond of the darker  and mischievous christmas stories  grilla is a giantess or troll who  originally was mentioned in the prose  edda but since has become associated  with christmas  her appearance is fairly repulsive a  giant hag who has a taste for children  in some stories she is a beggar who  roams the streets asking parents to give  her their misbehaving children this can  be avoided by chasing her off or by  simply giving her some food  originally grilla was said to live in a  small cottage but she was chased away by  the town forcing her to retreat to a  secluded cave only to then resurface  during the christmas period  she is able to tell when children have  been misbehaving and so when christmas  comes and she leaves her cave she knows  which children to target  throwing them into her giant bag and  taking them home to make some delicious  timmy stew  she also has 13 children known as the  yule lads and a pet cat known as the  you'll cat  now if you think someone like grilla  would have a regular run-of-the-mill cat  i'm afraid you are deeply mistaken the  yule cat was an enormous feline with  razor whiskers claws that could shred  through anything and just like its owner  a taste for human flesh  it roams the snowy countryside during  the winter looking for children to  devour who had not received any new  clothing during christmas  hence the tradition of families giving  each other new clothing as christmas  presents  as if someone like grilla wasn't enough  children were also told if they didn't  work hard enough throughout the year  they would also have to be worried about  being eaten by the yule cat  as these traditions became more child  friendly the story was slightly altered  those who didn't receive any new  clothing for christmas would instead  have their christmas feast stolen and  eaten by the yule cat  to complete our trio of icelandic  stories we have the thirteen sons of  grilla the yule lads or as i prefer to  call them the christmas mini mad lads  starting from the 12th of december each  night one of them arrives in town where  they remain for 13 days the last  arriving on christmas eve  these menaces are tricksters and their  names reflect how annoying they can be  candle stealer  window peeper sausage stealer pot  scraper and some of my personal  favorites window liquor and doorway  sniffer for the most part they go around  harassing people making a mess and being  as mischievous as possible  it's a tradition for children to leave  their shoes by a windowsill if those  children have been well behaved the yule  lads will leave them a present in their  shoes  those like timmy who have been not so  well behaved are left with a potato in  their shoe  originally the stories of the yule lads  were far more violent and gruesome  similar to stories of their mother but  over time they became more comical and  child friendly it's difficult to  describe how they appear the best i  could come up with is a mix between the  seven dwarfs and santa's elves only way  more chaotic  in italy there are stories of a woman  known as la bafana an old woman who  delivers presents to children similar to  santa claus but instead on the 5th of  january  the name befana is thought to derive  from epiphany with the feast of epiphany  taking place the day after she delivers  her presence her origin goes back to the  birth of jesus buffana was approached by  three wise men asking for directions  as she was known as the best housekeeper  in the village she offered for them to  stay the night having such a pleasant  stay the three wise men then offered  befana the chance to join them on their  journey however she respectfully  declined as she had too much to do  eventually changing her mind she set off  to find the three wise men and visit  baby jesus  she gathered all manner of presence to  take with her however her search was  unsuccessful  guided by the stars she visited the  homes of all the children she came  across giving them presents and hoping  to eventually find the baby jesus  and so it became tradition  the same time every year she set off  visiting the homes of children and  giving them presents however misbehaving  children would receive a lump of coal  just like timmy  bothana is often portrayed riding her  broomstick which throughout the year she  would use to clean her house however  during the christmas period it was her  preferred mode of transportation  similar to santa she entered the homes  through their chimneys and with her she  carried a large hamper packed full of  sweets and all manner of presents  a list of christmas creatures is never  complete without some grubby little  goblins  in greece and the balkans there are  stories of the kalikantseros  or the galaganzaros if you wanted  something closer to the original  these are essentially evil goblins who  live underground for most of the year  that is until the 12 days of christmas  where they surface to cause chaos and  kidnap children who were born on the 12  days of christmas  legend states they live underground  soaring away at the tree of life and its  roots trying to destroy everything  during the 12 days of christmas they  surface and remain above ground for 14  days which gives the tree enough time to  restore itself  in general they are a big nuisance they  want to enter your house cause a mess  and wreak havoc  it's also said that children born on the  12 days of christmas can see and talk to  these creatures with some even fearing  they could become one  to combat this parents would tie a small  string of garlic cloves to their child  as a repellent there are some other  precautions one can take to ensure their  house remains goblin-free burning things  in your fireplace will make your chimney  much harder to enter as the smoke acts  as a repellent  placing a colander outside your door  also works as they will feel compelled  to sit down and count every single hull  however with the number three being a  sacred number they cannot say it out  loud without bursting into flames and so  they will start over and over again  leaving them counting and distracted all  night  now i did ask some family members about  this legend in particular i was told it  was a fairly common tradition to throw a  specific type of sausage as well as a  dessert that is essentially deep fried  dough doubles onto your roof  this is done as somewhat of an offering  or distraction as once they are done  with the food they just go away  so if you ever see someone throwing  sausages onto their roof around  christmas time  i mean they're probably still crazy but  they could have a small goblin issue  and with that we end this holiday  special  hopefully you've enjoyed yourselves  merry christmas and happy holidays  as always  i've been your host mythology and  fiction explained  reminding you to stay away from anyone  called window licker or doorway sniffer  [Music]  you
 

